firedamp
========

Methane plume aggregator. Maps satellite-detected methane plumes
alongside O&G infrastructure from the OGIM database.

Live: https://research.datadesk.eco/firedamp/

Sources
-------
- Carbon Mapper  plume detections (API)
- IMEO / MARS    UNEP methane plume database (manual download)
- SRON           TROPOMI weekly plume CSVs (FTP)
- OGIM v2.7     global O&G infrastructure (Zenodo GeoPackage)

Setup
-----
Requires Python (managed with uv) and optionally ogr2ogr + tippecanoe
for rebuilding OGIM tiles.

    make vendor        download vendored JS/CSS/fonts
    make serve         dev server on :8000

    make data          fetch plume sources, build plumes.bin
    make ogim          OGIM GeoPackage -> PMTiles
    make ogim-upload   upload PMTiles to GCS
    make rebuild       full pipeline: data + ogim + upload

Architecture
------------
Static HTML/JS/CSS frontend using MapLibre GL. No build step, no npm.
Python scripts handle data fetching and binary encoding.

Deployed via GitHub Pages. Push to main triggers deploy.
OGIM PMTiles (~500 MB) served from Google Cloud Storage.

URL scheme
----------
Map position:     #map=<zoom>/<lat>/<lon>
Plume permalink:  #plume=<id>
Custom layers:    ?layer=<slug>

